94439fa5|1|1 month ago|0|1|N|Absolute rubbish!|I&rsquo;ve been using the Fastrack Revoltt XR1 for around 10 days, and overall, my experience has been just okay. Unfortunately, it didn&rsquo;t fully meet my expectations. The health sensors are not reliable. The watch sometimes continuously shows BP readings even when I&rsquo;m not wearing or using it. It also records sleep data even though I never wear the watch while sleeping. The step count also seems inaccurate. The button response is noticeably delayed, which can be frustrating during regular use. The battery backup and call quality are just okay&mdash;nothing particularly impressive. The sports and fitness tracking features also don&rsquo;t feel very reliable. At times, the watch even shows a high BP alert when it isn&rsquo;t being worn, which makes me question the accuracy of the health-monitoring features. Overall, after 10 days of use, I would rate it as just okay. If you mainly want a watch to check the time and date, it works fine. But if you&rsquo;re buying it specifically for accurate health and fitness tracking, I wouldn&rsquo;t say it meets expectations
