bdb207ae|2|1 month ago|0|1|R|Expected a better product|Very disappointing,  not recommended for gaming. I bought the EvoFox Shadow X Pro expecting a decent wireless gaming mouse, but unfortunately, it has been a frustrating experience. The Bluetooth mode has noticeable lag, making it practically useless for gaming. The wired mode and wireless adapter are better, but I still experienced random stuttering and pointer freezing, which is unacceptable for a gaming mouse. The software is another major disappointment. Instead of proper desktop software, EvoFox uses a browser-based solution. Button customisation doesn't reliably save, and even after changing the RGB settings, the changes don't actually apply to the mouse. What's the point of having customisation options if they don't work? For the price, I expected much better reliability. Don't buy this mouse just because it offers wireless connectivity and RGB. Those features mean very little when the basic functionality isn't reliable. The 2 stars are for working well with Adaptor and Wired mode My recommendation: Skip this one. Spend a little more and get a better mouse from a more reliable brand.
