10898449|1|2 months ago|2|1|N|Horrible|I purchased the **HP S1000 Wireless Mouse (Model: 7YA12PA#ACJ)** on **12 March 2026**, and this has been one of the most disappointing HP products I have ever used. I use the mouse only for **normal office work (around 8 hours a day)**. The biggest problem is its **extremely poor battery life**. A brand-new AA alkaline battery lasts only **10&ndash;15 days**. In the **last 25 days alone, I have already replaced two new branded batteries**, and both were completely drained. To make sure it wasn't a defective unit, **I got the mouse replaced through an HP Service Center. Unfortunately, the replacement unit has exactly the same issue. Even after replacement, the battery drain problem remains unchanged.** This means the problem is not limited to a single piece. Either the product has a serious design flaw or its power management is very poor. A wireless mouse from a reputed brand like HP should normally last for several months on a single battery under regular office use. Apart from the unnecessary battery expense, it is also very frustrating because the mouse suddenly stops working when the battery gets exhausted. Having to keep spare batteries all the time defeats the purpose of buying a wireless mouse. Over time, the cost of replacing batteries becomes much higher than expected. I wasted my time visiting the HP Service Center, expecting the replacement would solve the problem. Unfortunately, the replacement behaves exactly the same, which has completely destroyed my confidence in this product. **Pros:** * Comfortable to hold. * Cursor performance is decent. **Cons:** * Extremely poor battery backup (only 10&ndash;15 days). * Replacement from HP Service Center did not fix the issue. * High recurring battery cost. * Unreliable for daily office work. * Poor power management. * Not worth the money. I expected much better quality from HP. Based on my personal experience, I cannot recommend this mouse to anyone. Save your money and co