506080f6|4|6 months ago|3|1|H|Great for Charging, Mediocre for Data Transfer|Description: Just received this; I will use it for a month and then update the review if needed. I bought this primarily for the 100W SuperVOOC support, and on the charging front, it performs exactly as advertised. It triggers the fast charging on my device without any issues, and the build quality feels sturdy and premium for the price. However, if you are planning to use this for frequent file transfers, be aware of the limitations. I benchmarked the data speeds and consistently got around 2.85 MB/s (approx. 23.9 Mbps). This is significantly slower than high-end data cables, falling strictly into basic USB 2.0 territory. Pros: Excellent fast charging (100W/SuperVOOC compatible). Thick, durable cable design. Great value for money. Cons: Slow data transfer speeds (not ideal for moving large files/videos). Verdict: Perfect as a dedicated charging cable. If you need high-speed data syncing, you might want to look elsewhere.
